* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CHILD(userno)
*
* True if a phantom with that user number is running that was started by this process, false in every other case.  The
* answer is read from SYSTEM(1058), SYS$CHILDREN: the user numbers of this process's direct child phantoms.  The phantoms of
* another process are not seen, and neither is a phantom that has ended.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

function !child(userno)
$catalog !child

   kids = system(1058)                  ;* SYS$CHILDREN, field mark delimited
   u = userno + 0
   locate u in kids<0> setting p then return 1
   return 0
end

* END-CODE
